---
import LightboxImage from './LightboxImage.astro';
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import character1 from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/character.png';
import character2 from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/character2.png';
import character3 from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/character3.png';
import character4 from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/character4.png';
import character5 from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/character5.png';
import character6 from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/character6.png';
import mcFinal from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/mc-final-design.jpg';
import mcColorVariation from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/mc-color-variation.png';
import referencesTogether from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/references-together.png';
import silhouettes from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/silhoettes.png';
import finalSketch from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/final-sketch-web.jpg';
import finalLine from '@assets/sanctuary/characters/final-line.png';
---

<section class="character-design" id="character-design">
  <SectionHeading eyebrow="Character Design Approach" title="Character Design" />

  <p class="intro">
    The core challenge was designing three distinct character identities: two settlement groups shaped
    by different values, and an outsider protagonist. Each needed to read as clearly different at a
    glance. At the same time, all three had to feel like they belong to the same visual world.
  </p>

  <div class="group-block">
    <h3>Main Character</h3>
    <p class="quote">"When I need to design something unusual, I like to rely on nature."</p>
    <p class="body">
      Unique palette and materials, unused by either group — visually marks them as an outsider
      arriving from beyond the settlement.
    </p>
    <div class="image-row">
      <LightboxImage src={mcFinal} alt="Main character final design" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="group-block two-col">
    <div>
      <h3>Spirit Group</h3>
      <p class="body">
        Warm, natural palette with purple accents that intensify with status. Rounded, organic forms
        with growing ornamentation by rank. Natural materials: fabric, wood, occasional tech elements
        tied to profession.
      </p>
      <div class="image-row two">
        <LightboxImage src={character3} alt="Spirit group character study" />
        <LightboxImage src={character4} alt="Spirit group character study" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Mind Group</h3>
      <p class="body">
        Cold blue palette, sharp geometric forms. Functional, tech-driven design. Materials: metal,
        polymers, plastic. Defining trait: a head suspended by a thick cable.
      </p>
      <div class="image-row two">
        <LightboxImage src={character5} alt="Mind group character study" />
        <LightboxImage src={character6} alt="Mind group character study" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="process-grid">
    <div class="process-item">
      <p class="label">References</p>
      <Image src={referencesTogether} alt="Character references" widths={[500, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="process-item">
      <p class="label">Silhouette Search</p>
      <Image src={silhouettes} alt="Silhouette exploration" widths={[500, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="process-item">
      <p class="label">Color Search</p>
      <Image src={mcColorVariation} alt="Color variation exploration" widths={[500, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="process-item">
      <p class="label">Faces</p>
      <LightboxImage src={character1} alt="Face studies" />
    </div>
    <div class="process-item">
      <p class="label">Final Sketch</p>
      <Image src={finalSketch} alt="Final sketch" widths={[500, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="process-item">
      <p class="label">Final Line</p>
      <Image src={finalLine} alt="Final line art" widths={[500, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="process-item">
      <p class="label">Final</p>
      <LightboxImage src={character2} alt="Final character render" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .character-design {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 60ch;
    color: #c9c9c9;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .group-block {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .group-block h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    color: #e8e8e8;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .quote {
    font-style: italic;
    color: #9a9a9a;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .body {
    color: #c9c9c9;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .image-row {
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    max-width: 500px;
  }

  .image-row.two {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .two-col {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .process-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .process-item .label {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: #9a9a9a;
  }

  .process-item :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 4px;
    display: block;
  }
</style>
